{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the fountains were stopped, etc.</b> The verse alludes to the nature of rains and their force: for when the waters descend from above, the lower waters necessarily rise to meet them, and one is not found without the other. This is what the verse means when it says <b>and they were stopped</b>, etc., <b>and the rain was restrained</b> — for these two kinds of water function as one. And so it is in the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Ta'anit 25b): no drop descends from above unless two drops rise to meet it from below, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:06.564966978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}